9^400 - 1)/8 ≡ 9 * 2000 = 18000 mod 10000 ≡ 8000.\n\nWait, let me double check. (9^400 - 1)/8 mod 10000. We have 9^400 - 1 ≡ 16000 mod 80000. So (9^400-1)/8 ≡ 2000 mod 10000. Then N = 9 * 2000 = 18000 ≡ 8000 mod 10000.\n\nSo the last four digits are 8000.\n\nLet me verify with a small check. Let me verify the formula and a small case.\n\nActually, let me double-check by computing N mod 10000 more directly for a smaller case to validate the method, then trust the computation.\n\nLet me verify 9^400 mod 80000 = 16001 by checking mod 128 and mod 625 again.\n\nmod 128: 9^16 ≡ 1, 400 = 16*25, so 9^400 ≡ 1. ✓\nmod 625: got 376. Let me re-verify 9^400 mod 625.\n\nLet me recompute more carefully.\n9^2 = 81\n9^4 = 6561 mod 625 = 6561 - 6250 = 311 ✓\n9^8 = 311^2 = 96721. 625*154 = 96250. 96721-96250 = 471 ✓\n9^16 = 471^2 = 221841. 625*354 = 221250. 221841-221250 = 591 ✓\n9^32 = 591^2 = 349281. 625*558 = 348750. 349281-348750 = 531 ✓\n9^64 = 531^2 = 281961. 625*451 = 281875. 281961-281875 = 86 ✓\n9^128 = 86^2 = 7396. 625*11 = 6875. 7396-6875 = 521 ✓\n9^256 = 521^2 = 271441. 625*434 = 271250. 271441-271250 = 191 ✓\n\n400 = 256+128+16: 191 * 521 mod 625:\n191*521: 191*500 = 95500, 191*21 = 4011, total 99511. 99511 mod 625: 625*159 = 99375, 99511-99375 = 136 ✓\n136 * 591 = 136*591. 136*591 = 136*600 - 136*9 = 81600 - 1224 = 80376. 80376 mod 625: 625*128 = 80000, 80376-80000 = 376 ✓\n\nCRT: x ≡ 1 mod 128, x ≡ 376 mod 625.\n128a + 1 ≡ 376 → 128a ≡ 375 mod 625.\n128^{-1} mod 625 = 542 (verified via extended Euclidean).\na ≡ 375 * 542 mod 625.\n375 * 542: 375*500 = 187500, 375*42 = 15750, total 203250. 203250 mod 625: 625*325 = 203125, remainder 125. a = 125.\nx = 128*125 + 1 = 16001. ✓\n\nSo 9^400 mod 80000 = 16001.\n9^400 - 1 = 16000 mod 80000.\n(9^400-1)/8 = 2000 mod 10000.\nN = 9 * 2000 = 18000 mod 10000 = 8000.\n\nThe last four digits are 8000.\n\nLet me sanity check with a tiny example: 9^1 + 9^2 = 9 + 81 = 90. Formula: 9(9^2-1)/8 = 9*80/8 = 90. ✓\n\nAnother: 9^1+9^2+9^3 = 9+81+729 = 819. Formula: 9(9^3-1)/8 = 9*728/8 = 9*91 = 819. ✓\n\nGood. The answer is 8000.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786689369}
